{
  "requirement": "requirements.ci.errors",
  "file": "src/evidence.rs",
  "item": "fn[inspect_repository_with_progress]",
  "queries": [
    "early_exits",
    "error_accumulators"
  ],
  "applies": true,
  "fixmes": [],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`src/evidence.rs#fn[inspect_repository_with_progress]` is a site because it declares a local `let mut errors = Vec::new()` and sequences the repository checks.\n\n**Continuation after failures.** Each check records its failure in `errors` and the function moves on:\n- `load_workspace_evidence` failures are pushed and the function continues.\n- `book_source_dir` falls back to `md` on a malformed `book.toml`. It records one error and returns, so `collect_definitions` still runs.\n- `validate_setup`, the evidence-file loop, the missing-evidence loop, reference discovery, `validate_committed_credentials`, `sites::discover`, `validate_references`, `citations::validate`, `sites::validate` and both `rust_coverage` validators all run unconditionally, each writing into the same `errors`.\n- The evidence-file loop has no `continue` or `break`. `validate_evidence_file` runs for every file, including after the \"no matching requirement or example\" push.\n- The only checks skipped are those that depend on a failed result, such as a definition missing from `present`. That is the allowed dependence.\n\n**Violation match `fs::canonicalize(root)?`.** This is harmless. It runs before `errors` exists and before any check has failed. Every later check depends on a resolvable root, so no independent check is skipped. It is a precondition failure of the whole inspection, not a failed check followed by an early exit.\n\n**Duplicate reports.** I found none in the code I read.\n- `load_workspace_evidence` and `workspace_document` read `habeas.toml`.\n- `book_source_dir` reads `book.toml`.\n- `validate_setup` and `workspace_root` read `Cargo.toml` and `.config/nextest.toml`.\n- Because these read different files, one failure is not reported by two of them.\n- Reference-discovery errors are also copied into `discovery_errors`. That is a separate vector from `errors`, so it does not duplicate entries in the report.\n\nThe site meets the obligations of `requirements.ci.errors`.",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "file": "src/evidence.rs",
      "item": "fn[inspect_repository_with_progress]",
      "hash": "788e24af357372441e74b0823319d6b50ee4c071637fc9a47eb30d05e94d654d"
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.ci.errors",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.ci.errors"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::::{req} errors",
        "Repository validation MUST continue after a failed check and report every failed",
        "check it finds in one run, each as a {term}`requirements.ci.validation_error`.",
        "This is a convention for every validation error; the requirement for each check",
        "states which conditions that check reports. A file that cannot be parsed, such as",
        "a malformed `habeas.toml`, `book.toml`, or evidence file, is one failed check:",
        "its error MAY report only the first parse or decoding problem in that file, and",
        "checks that do not depend on its contents MUST still run.",
        "",
        "The code that sequences the repository's checks carries out the first paragraph.",
        "A repository-validation function that collects validation errors MUST hold them",
        "in a parameter or local variable named `errors`, and a function with such a",
        "variable is a site below; authoring code that collects errors only to abort is",
        "not one. After one of its checks fails, a site MUST still run every later check",
        "that does not depend on the failed check's result, including later checks in the",
        "same loop iteration, and MUST NOT report one failure twice.",
        "",
        "::::{sites} error_accumulators",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src, crates/habeas-sdk/src]",
        "exclude: [src/authoring/inputs.rs, src/authoring/tools.rs]",
        "rule:",
        "  kind: function_item",
        "  has:",
        "    stopBy: { kind: function_item }",
        "    any:",
        "      - kind: parameter",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "      - kind: let_declaration",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "  not:",
        "    inside:",
        "      stopBy: end",
        "      kind: mod_item",
        "      has: { field: name, regex: \"^tests$\" }",
        "match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut errors: BTreeSet<String> = BTreeSet::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut errors);",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, discovery_errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut problems = Vec::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut problems);",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    mod tests {",
        "        fn check(errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        "",
        "::::{violations} early_exits",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src, crates/habeas-sdk/src]",
        "within: error_accumulators",
        "rule:",
        "  any:",
        "    - kind: try_expression",
        "    - kind: return_expression",
        "    - kind: continue_expression",
        "    - kind: break_expression",
        "match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); continue; }",
        "            if item.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        if !v.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); return; }",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); break; }",
        "        }",
        "        if items.is_empty() { errors.push(\"empty\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn parse(v: &Value) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        ":::::"
      ]
    },
